From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Patrick Quinn <patrick.jm.quinn@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 13:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] media: mediatek: isp6s: camsv: Turn the clocks off on removal

The driver core drops its runtime PM reference before calling
.remove(), but with autosuspend in use that only schedules the
suspend. mtk_camsv_remove() then disabled runtime PM, which cancelled
it, and left the device active with its clocks enabled; its own
pm_runtime_put_autosuspend() had no reference to drop and only logged
"Runtime PM usage count underflow!".

The CAM power domain then went off and reset the CAMSYS clock gates,
while the clock framework still counted them as enabled. After the
driver was bound again, enabling the clocks only raised their counts,
the gates stayed closed, and the first stream failed with "larb13
port 6 stays in MMU mode" because larb13 ignored the write. The
enable counts of all five CAMSYS clocks and the CAMTM mux stayed at 1
after unloading the module, with the domain off.

Stop autosuspend, disable runtime PM and run the runtime suspend
callback if the device is still active, so that the clocks are turned
off while the domain is still on, and drop the unbalanced put.

Signed-off-by: Patrick Quinn <patrick.jm.quinn@gmail.com>
---
 camsv/mtk_camsv_hw.c | 5 ++++-
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/camsv/mtk_camsv_hw.c b/camsv/mtk_camsv_hw.c
index a4c0688..5339c6d 100644
--- a/camsv/mtk_camsv_hw.c
+++ b/camsv/mtk_camsv_hw.c
@@ -603,8 +603,11 @@ static void mtk_camsv_remove(struct platform_device *pdev)
 	struct mtk_cam_dev *cam_dev = dev_get_drvdata(dev);
 
 	mtk_isp6s_camsv_dev_cleanup(cam_dev);
-	pm_runtime_put_autosuspend(dev);
+	pm_runtime_dont_use_autosuspend(dev);
 	pm_runtime_disable(dev);
+	if (!pm_runtime_status_suspended(dev))
+		mtk_camsv_runtime_suspend(dev);
+	pm_runtime_set_suspended(dev);
 }
 
 static const struct dev_pm_ops mtk_camsv_pm_ops = {
-- 
2.55.0

